Source: velocity-init
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Maintainer: velocity-init developers <maintainer@example.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper (>= 13), cargo (>= 1.60)
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Rules-Requires-Root: binary-targets

Package: velocity-init
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends},
         initramfs-tools | initramfs-tools-core,
         adduser
Recommends: procps, kbd
Description: A modern dependency-based init system and service manager
 velocity-init is a lightweight alternative to sysvinit and systemd,
 implemented in Rust as a supervised PID 1.
 .
 It boots LSB-header init scripts in parallel according to a dependency
 DAG, supervises services with crash detection and exponential-backoff
 restarts, scopes processes in cgroups v2, supports socket activation,
 and acts as a full /etc/inittab drop-in for Devuan (telinit, runlevel,
 who -r, ctrl-alt-del and power-failure signals).
 .
 This package installs the static binary to /sbin/velocity-init and adds
 an initramfs-tools hook so it can be selected with init=/sbin/velocity-init
 on the kernel command line.